where applicable.'],                                ['@type' => 'HowToStep', 'name' => 'Set the size and resolution', 'text' => 'For printed labels, set the resolution to 300 DPI and choose a width and height that fits your label stock.'],                                ['@type' => 'HowToStep', 'name' => 'Download and print', 'text' => 'Download as PNG, SVG or JPG, then print at 100% scale (no "fit to page") to keep the barcode scannable.'],                            ],                        ],                    ],                ],            ],            'static_html' => '<main style="font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:760px;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;line-height:1.6">'                . '<nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/tools">Tools</a> &rsaquo; Barcode Generator</nav>'                . '<h1>Free Barcode Generator</h1>'                . '<p><strong>The VenQore Barcode Generator creates print-ready barcodes in 9 formats — Code128, Code39, Code93, EAN-13, EAN-8, UPC-A, UPC-E, ITF-14 and Codabar.</strong> It outputs PNG, SVG or JPG at up to 300 DPI, computes check digits automatically, and is free to use with no signup and no watermark.</p>'                . '<h2>Supported formats</h2>'                . '<table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Character set</th><th>Length</th><th>Typical retail use</th></tr></thead><tbody>' . $formatTableRows . '</tbody></table>'                . '<h2>Which barcode should I use?</h2>'                . '<p>Use <strong>EAN-13</strong> if you sell internationally or outside North America. Use <strong>UPC-A</strong> if you sell primarily in the United States or Canada. Use <strong>Code128</strong> for internal inventory codes, asset tags, or serial numbers that are not retail point-of-sale products. Use <strong>ITF-14</strong> for shipping cartons and case-level packaging rather than individual items.</p>'                . '<h2>How to print barcode labels</h2>'                . '<ol><li>Choose the format that matches your use case.</li><li>Enter your value — the tool validates length and computes the check digit automatically.</li><li>Set resolution to 300 DPI for print.</li><li>Download as PNG or SVG and print at 100% scale.</li></ol>'                . '<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>'                . implode('', array_map(fn ($qa) => "<p><strong>{$qa[0]}</strong> {$qa[1]}</p>", $barcodeFaqs))                . '<h2>More barcode formats</h2><ul>'                . implode('', array_map(                    fn ($slug, $f) => "<li><a href=\"/tools/barcode-generator/{$slug}\">{$f[0]} Generator</a></li>",                    array_keys($formats),                    $formats                ))                . '</ul>'                . self::toolCta('barcodes')                . '<p>Related: <a href="/tools/barcode-validator">Barcode Check Digit Validator</a></p>'                . $nav . '</main>',        ];
        // ── Format children ──
        // tools.barcode.format is ONE Laravel route (GET /barcode-generator/{format})
        // shared across all 9 symbologies, so these are keyed
        // "route.name:{format}" — see MarketingSeo::current()'s parameterised
        // lookup, which resolves Route::current()->parameters()['format']
