only used for {$use}. Fun fact: {$fact}</p>"                    . "<h2>About {$name}</h2><p>{$name} supports {$charset} at {$length}. It is typically used for {$use}.</p>"                    . '<h2>How to generate a ' . $name . ' barcode</h2>'                    . "<ol><li>Enter a value that matches {$name}'s character set and length rules.</li><li>Preview updates live as you type.</li><li>Download as PNG or SVG at up to 300 DPI.</li></ol>"                    . "<p><a href=\"/tools/barcode-generator\">&larr; Back to all barcode formats</a></p>"                    . self::toolCta('barcodes')                    . $nav . '</main>',            ];        }
        // ── T10 Validator ──
        $validatorFaqs = [            ['What is a barcode check digit?', 'A check digit is the final digit of a barcode, calculated from the preceding digits using a modulo-10 algorithm. Scanners use it to detect misreads — if the check digit does not match, the scan is rejected.'],            ['How is the UPC/EAN check digit calculated?', 'Starting from the rightmost digit, alternating digits are multiplied by 3 and 1, the results are summed, and the check digit is the number that brings that sum to the next multiple of 10.'],            ['What is a GTIN?', 'GTIN (Global Trade Item Number) is the umbrella standard covering UPC-A (GTIN-12), EAN-13 (GTIN-13) and ITF-14 (GTIN-14) — this validator normalizes any of them to their 14-digit GTIN form.'],        ];
        $pages['tools.barcode-validator'] = [            'title'       => 'UPC/EAN Barcode Check Digit Validator — Free | VenQore',            'description' => 'Validate any UPC, EAN or GTIN barcode number free. See the computed check digit and the full modulo-10 arithmetic breakdown. No signup.',            'keywords'    => 'upc check digit calculator, ean 13 check digit, validate barcode number, gtin validator, barcode checksum calculator',            'jsonld'      => [                [                    '@context' => 'https://schema.org',                    '@graph'   => [                        self::softwareApplicationLd(                            'VenQore Barcode Validator',                            url('/tools/barcode-validator'),                            'Free UPC/EAN/GTIN check digit validator with full modulo-10 arithmetic breakdown.'                        ),                        self::breadcrumbLd([                            ['name' => 'Home', 'url' => url('/')],                            ['name' => 'Tools', 'url' => url('/tools')],                            ['name' => 'Barcode Validator', 'url' => url('/tools/barcode-validator')],                        ]),                        self::faqLd($validatorFaqs),                    ],                ],            ],            'static_html' => '<main style="font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:760px;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;line-height:1.6">'                . '<nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/tools">Tools</a> &rsaquo; Barcode Validator</nav>'                . '<h1>UPC / EAN / GTIN Barcode Check Digit Validator</h1>'                . '<p><strong>Paste any GTIN-8, GTIN-12 (UPC-A), GTIN-13 (EAN-13) or GTIN-14 (ITF-14) number to check whether its check digit is valid.</strong> The tool shows the computed check digit and the full modulo-10 arithmetic, free, with no signup.</p>'                . '<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>'                . implode('', array_map(fn ($qa) => "<p><strong>{$qa[0]}</strong> {$qa[1]}</p>", $validatorFaqs))                . '<p><a href="/tools/barcode-generator">Generate a new barcode &rarr;</a></p>'                . $nav . '</main>',        ];
        return $pages;    }

