                            ['@type' => 'HowToStep', 'name' => 'Add products', 'text' => 'Add rows manually or bulk-paste a list as name,sku,unit,category — one product per line.'],                                    ['@type' => 'HowToStep', 'name' => 'Tag category or aisle', 'text' => 'Optionally tag each row with a category or aisle/location so the printed sheet groups items the way you actually walk the floor.'],                                    ['@type' => 'HowToStep', 'name' => 'Choose orientation and download', 'text' => 'Pick Portrait or Landscape, then download the finished PDF — grouped by category, with blank Counted Qty and Variance columns ready for staff to fill in by hand.'],                                ],                            ],                        ],                    ],                ],                'static_html' => '<main style="font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:760px;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;line-height:1.6">'                    . '<nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/tools">Tools</a> &rsaquo; Stock Count Sheet</nav>'                    . '<h1>Free Stock Count Sheet Generator</h1>'                    . '<p><strong>Create a printable, unwatermarked PDF stock count sheet for physical inventory counts.</strong> Add products manually or bulk-paste a list, group and sub-header rows by category or aisle so the sheet matches how you actually walk the floor, and print with blank Counted Qty and Variance columns for staff to fill in by hand. No signup, no limit on products or pages.</p>'                    . '<h2>What you can customize</h2>'                    . '<ul><li>Business name, logo, location/warehouse, counted-by name, date and count reference number</li>'                    . '<li>Unlimited product rows with name, SKU/barcode (optional), unit (each, box, kg, etc.) and category/aisle tag</li>'                    . '<li>Bulk CSV paste: one product per line as name,sku,unit,category</li>'                    . '<li>Automatic grouping and sub-headers by category or location, with uncategorized items collected at the end</li>'                    . '<li>Optional SKU/barcode text column</li>'                    . '<li>Portrait or Landscape orientation</li>'                    . '<li>Blank write-in Counted Qty and Variance columns per row, plus a Discrepancy Notes section</li>'                    . '<li>Page numbering ("Page X of Y") for multi-page sheets</li></ul>'                    . '<h2>Why a physical count matters even with a POS system</h2>'                    . '<p>A point-of-sale system only knows what it was told — sales, purchases, and manual adjustments. It cannot see theft, breakage, spoilage, receiving errors, or staff mistakes. A physical stock count is the only way to find the real gap between what your system expects and what is actually on the shelf, which is what a variance report and your accountant both need at period end.</p>'                    . '<h2>How to organize a count by location</h2>'                    . '<p>Walk your floor or warehouse in a fixed order — aisle by aisle, shelf by shelf — and tag each product row with that aisle or category before generating the sheet. The PDF automatically groups and sub-headers rows to match, so whoever is holding the clipboard never has to hunt for the next item.</p>'                    . '<h2>How to create a stock count sheet</h2>'                    . '<ol><li>Add your store details — saved locally for next time.</li><li>Add products manually or bulk-paste a CSV-style list.</li><li>Tag rows with a category or aisle for floor-order grouping.</li><li>Pick Portrait or Landscape and download the PDF.</li></ol>'                    . '<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>'                    . implode('', array_map(fn ($qa) => "<p><strong>{$qa[0]}</strong> {$qa[1]}</p>", $stockFaqs))                    . self::toolCta('inventory counts')                    . '<p>Related: <a href="/tools/bar